{
  "about": "Boundary vectors for the D5 metadata limits. Each case is run through the zod input schema (limit-vectors.test.ts) and through PostgreSQL via the Data API (@synapcity/server-data, test:db), so the two cannot drift. `value` is a string, an array (tags), or a generator: {repeat, times, prefix, suffix} builds the repeated text; {distinct} builds that many different tags; {units} builds a string from UTF-16 code units (how an unpaired surrogate is written, which JSON tooling will not carry as an escape). `zod` is the outcome of the input schema (which trims names and tags; `zodOutput` is what it keeps when that differs from `value`); `db` is the outcome of inserting `value` as given. They differ only where the app normalizes first, or is deliberately stricter than the database (control characters, direction-changing characters, invisible-only text), and each such case says why in `note`. Lengths count code points. The file is ASCII-escaped on purpose: it holds invisible characters and unpaired surrogates.",
